 # Migrations
 
+## Feed and join dynamics extraction (2026-11-12)
+
+Import constant-feed, acceleration-limited, symmetric-jerk, corner-limit and
+lookahead operations and their reports from `hyperdynamics`. Aggregate feed
+operations consume `MetricPath`; span scheduling consumes `MetricSpan` and
+`JoinSpan`. Native slices, arrays and vectors of metric spans supply aggregate
+length without copying geometry. Join providers retain complete source-owned
+receipts in `ClassifiedJoin`; lower reports are generic over that receipt.
+For Hyperpath sources, the receipt is `hyperpath::TangentJoinReport`.
+
+Hyperpath preserves its old concrete report aliases and deprecated function
+paths through a coordinated minor release. Its old line-only feed operations
+still require axis-aligned geometry through a borrowed metric adapter; mixed
+`FeedPathElement` paths retain Euclidean/symbolic lengths. The `_for_path`
+compatibility functions delegate to the corresponding unsuffixed Hyperdynamics
+operation. Old feed-equation builders also remain deprecated wrappers.
+
+Validation, length and tangent query order, repeated replay, error boundaries
+and canonical application fields retain their existing contracts. The current
+extraction remains pending its cost qualification; see the interval progress
+ledger for demonstrated coverage and open gates.
+
+## Exact metric and jerk dynamics extraction (2026-11-12)
+
+Import `plan_monotonic_jerk_transition`, `certify_jerk_ramp_feed_schedule`,
+`certify_multi_phase_jerk_ramp_feed_schedule` and their report/proposal types
+from `hyperdynamics`. They consume `MetricSpan`; Hyperpath implements that trait
+for `FeedPathElement` using its retained exact length authority. The old concrete
+entry points and type paths remain available for at least one coordinated minor
+release, with deprecated functions preserving `RouteCertificationError`.
+Conversions between that error and `DynamicsError` preserve every variant.
+
+Length acquisition remains lazy, including its error precedence and repeated
+replay queries. No lengths are sampled or rounded. Solver reports and application
+evidence encodings retain their existing fields. Shared public `check_*` input
+checks retain predicate certainty, stage, and refinement requirements; the
+compatibility schedulers keep their existing flattened unresolved-error contract.
+The feed/lookahead migration is described above; performance qualification
+remains open.
+
+## Affine axis dynamics extraction (2026-11-12)
+
+Hyperdynamics 0.1 owns affine axis-limit selection and replay. Import
+`plan_axis_projected_motion_limits`, `certify_axis_projected_motion_limits`
+and their reports from `hyperdynamics`. Hyperpath 0.3 retains its existing type
+reexports and deprecated function wrappers through at least one coordinated
+minor release. Those wrappers preserve `RouteCertificationError`; new callers
+receive `DynamicsError`. `RouteCertificationError::from` maps every current
+dynamics variant explicitly for existing application error boundaries.
+
+Exact values, row order, bottlenecks and solver reports retain their meaning.
+No canonical encoding changes. Feed/lookahead compatibility is described above; qualification remains open.
+
